X86: project canonical EVEX register scans without operands

Derive compact public-ID and length plans from the existing full-decoder
probes, sharing reserved-field admission with the vector output path.
Complete unprefixed register forms avoid operand construction when both
text and detail are disabled; adapters and all misses retain their current
precedence and fallback. Keep the new code and data in separate sections
on ELF x86-64 full userspace builds.
